# Exit Sign, by GPT-6.1-sol & SZ. Original Alt rock / pop punk: a vocal-style fuzz hook,
# palm-muted verses, full guitar-wall choruses, and a drumless drop into a half-time bridge.
# Built by tools/arranger/exit-sign.mjs from hand-composed melodies and one harmonic map.
# Each chord below lasts one bar; every pitched part stays on that bar's chord tones.
# Chords intro: G | C | D | G
# Chords verse: Em | C | G | D | Em | C | Am | D | Em | C | G | D | Em | C | Am | D
# Chords pre: Am | C | Em | D | Am | C | D | D
# Chords chorus: G | C | Em | D | G | Am | C | D | Em | C | D | G
# Chords bridge: C | C | Am | Am | Em | Em | D | D
# Chords outro: G | C | D | G
# Form 1-4: intro - Intro: clean strings, then the band counts itself in
# Form 5-20: verse - Verse 1: palm-muted, with room between vocal phrases
# Form 21-28: pre - Pre-chorus 1: eighths open up; a tom fill opens the door
# Form 29-40: chorus - Chorus 1: the twelve-bar hook
# Form 41-56: verse - Verse 2: a new vocal phrasing, then ride cymbal
# Form 57-64: pre - Pre-chorus 2: rebuilding the same tension
# Form 65-76: chorus - Chorus 2: full band, then the floor drops away
# Form 77-84: bridge - Bridge: two bars without bass or drums, then a half-time backbeat
# Form 85-96: chorus - Final chorus A: back to full time, with clean-guitar answers
# Form 97-108: chorus - Final chorus B: the hook stays put; the final tonic gets its whole beat
# Form 109-112: outro - Outro: the opening syllables return, then one last band chord
# The snare drags 12 ticks (18 in half time); guitar chugs trail the kick by 10 ticks.
# Kick-locked bass eighths and louder cymbals make the chorus lift; no fixed bank instruments.
title: Exit Sign
composer: GPT-6.1-sol & SZ
year: 2026
source: original
category: originals
style: altrock
key: G major
tempo: 152
time: 4/4
about: One more chorus before the lights come up: palm-muted verses give way to a twelve-bar shout-along hook, the band drops out for a half-time bridge, and the final double chorus finds its way home.

